<title>USA: Rubin - administration opposes U.S. House tax bill.</title>
<headline>Rubin - administration opposes U.S. House tax bill.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Clinton administration &quot;strongly opposes&quot; tax legislation being debated by the House of Representatives Thursday, Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said in a letter.</p>
<p>In a letter to House Speaker Newt Gingrich, a Georgia Republican, Rubin said the House bill failed to meet conditions set in last month's budget agreement between congressional leaders and the White House.</p>
</text>
